If you mean Niri keybinds for controlling Noctalia, add these inside binds {} in ~/.config/niri/config.kdl:
kdl

Mod+Space { spawn-sh "noctalia msg panel-toggle launcher"; }
Mod+S { spawn-sh "noctalia msg panel-toggle control-center"; }
Mod+Comma { spawn-sh "noctalia msg settings-toggle"; }

XF86AudioRaiseVolume { spawn-sh "noctalia msg volume-up"; }
XF86AudioLowerVolume { spawn-sh "noctalia msg volume-down"; }
XF86AudioMute { spawn-sh "noctalia msg volume-mute"; }
XF86MonBrightnessUp { spawn-sh "noctalia msg brightness-up"; }
XF86MonBrightnessDown { spawn-sh "noctalia msg brightness-down"; }

Here Mod is usually the Super/Windows key. Noctalia’s Niri docs list these IPC bindings; reload Niri after editing your config. noctalia.dev

Common Niri keys in a CachyOS/Noctalia setup include Mod+Return for terminal, Mod+Ctrl+Return for launcher, Mod+1…9 for workspaces, and Mod+Shift+Escape for the hotkey overlay. Your exact bindings depend on your config. 
